      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "Tylocrebrine, a related polycyclic methoxy-substituted alkaloid, showed rapid brain accumulation with an AUCbrain of 2.1 µg·h/mL in mice, supporting CNS access for this alkaloid family.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "N-propylnorapomorphine, a tetrahydroisoquinoline/aporphine alkaloid, demonstrated good brain penetration in rats and nonhuman primates by PET, supporting CNS access for related isoquinoline scaffolds.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "The methoxy-substituted aromatic ligand [11C]SA4503 showed high and receptor-specific brain uptake in rats, illustrating that this type of lipophilic alkaloid-like structure achieves meaningful CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is noscapine, a phthalideisoquinoline alkaloid. Multiple structurally related isoquinoline/protoberberine/aporphine alkaloids are directly detected in brain or CSF or show high brain uptake, and noscapine itself is known to cross the BBB; therefore meaningful CNS access is predicted.",
